(their grammatical agreement and semantic polarity.) Tj
T*
(Answer: \(1\) Syntactic category: 'Few' and 'A few' modify plural COUNTABLE nouns and take) Tj
T*
(plural verbs; 'Little' and 'A little' modify UNCOUNTABLE \(mass\) nouns and take singular) Tj
T*
(verbs. \(2\) Semantic Polarity: Bare 'few' and 'little' convey a NEGATIVE meaning) Tj
T*
(equivalent to 'almost none', 'scarcely any', or 'insufficient'. They emphasize deficit) Tj
T*
(or absence \(e.g., 'Few cells survived' = nearly all died; 'There is little hope' =) Tj
T*
(virtually hopeless\). In contrast, 'a few' and 'a little' convey a POSITIVE meaning) Tj
T*
(equivalent to 'some' or 'a small but adequate quantity' \(e.g., 'A few cells survived' =) Tj
T*
(a positive count is alive and cultivable; 'There is a little broth left' = some broth) Tj
T*
(remains\).) Tj
T*
